From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:26:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban tests: pin worker_session_id on
 kanban_continue and kanban_request_review

Problem: the _LOST_REVIEW_KEYS comment says kanban_continue and kanban_request_review
stamp worker_session_id like kanban_complete does, but no test exercised either path.
Removing both stamps (tools/kanban_tools.py:1220 and :1285) still passed 371 tests in
11 kanban files (exact-head Opus review of 2e4dae31afa0).

Why 1: the previous commit pinned only kanban_complete, the path the lost-review
incident used.
Why 2: the comment was widened to name the other two worker tools from reading the
code, without a test for each newly named entry path.
Root: a claim about N entry paths needs N entry-path tests; the comment named three
tools and the tests covered one.

Fix: test_continue_and_request_review_stamp_worker_session_id[continue|request_review]
calls each tool handler as a dispatcher worker (HERMES_KANBAN_TASK, HERMES_KANBAN_RUN_ID,
HERMES_SESSION_ID) and reads the metadata of the run the tool ended.

Proof (hermes-core-wt test, hub): the no_verdict file has 56 passed. Removing the stamp at
:1220 fails exactly [continue], at :1285 exactly [request_review], and both together fail
exactly those two (54 passed).
---
 ...est_kanban_dependency_review_no_verdict.py | 23 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_dependency_review_no_verdict.py b/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_dependency_review_no_verdict.py
index 71a7715379..7a25cad982 100644
--- a/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_dependency_review_no_verdict.py
+++ b/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_dependency_review_no_verdict.py
@@ -210,6 +210,29 @@ def test_lost_review_completed_by_the_worker_tool_stays_held(board, monkeypatch)
     assert dispatch.check_respawn_guard(board, task) == "active_pr"
 
 
+@pytest.mark.parametrize("tool", ["continue", "request_review"])
+def test_continue_and_request_review_stamp_worker_session_id(board, monkeypatch, tool):
+    """The _LOST_REVIEW_KEYS comment says kanban_continue and kanban_request_review stamp worker_session_id
+    like kanban_complete does; pin each of those entry paths on the run the tool ends."""
+    from tools import kanban_tools as kt
+    _task, parents = incident(board, monkeypatch, finish=False)
+    parent = parents[0]
+    kb.claim_task(board, parent)
+    row = kb.get_task(board, parent)
+    assert row is not None and row.current_run_id
+    monkeypatch.setenv("HERMES_KANBAN_TASK", parent)
+    monkeypatch.setenv("HERMES_KANBAN_RUN_ID", str(row.current_run_id))
+    monkeypatch.setenv("HERMES_SESSION_ID", "review-session")
+    if tool == "continue":
+        out = json.loads(kt._handle_continue({"checkpoint": "Reviewed half of PR #682; next: the tests."}))
+    else:
+        out = json.loads(kt._handle_request_review({"summary": "Reviewed PR #682. No blocking defects."}))
+    assert out["ok"] is True, out
+    stored = kb._json_dict(board.execute(
+        "SELECT metadata FROM task_runs WHERE id = ?", (row.current_run_id,)).fetchone()[0])
+    assert stored.get("worker_session_id") == "review-session", stored
+
+
